    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d312">

                <pb facs="0414" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg404"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12–1747: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-12-17T12:00:00+08:00">December 17,
                            1947—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received December 17—4:12 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2408. Carson Chang left Shanghai Dec. 13 by air for US. Reliable American
                    controlled source close Chang states Chang’s only purpose present visit is
                    attempt interview Secretary State and George Kennan<anchor n="91"
                        xml:id="d312-f1"/> and that he is using University Washington lectureship as
                    blind. Source further states Chang asserts to Chinese friends only posts he
                    would accept in Chinese Govt are President or Vice-President.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d312-f1" n="91" xml:id="d312-f1-content">
